<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Salassi</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 25 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alpine people of the Aosta valley who controlled the Great and Little St Bernard passes and their gold, and resisted Rome until 25 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Salassi lived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aosta-valley">Aosta valley</a> and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Eporedia</a> (Ivrea), at the foot of the passes over the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. Ancient writers called them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a>, though they probably mixed with earlier Ligurian peoples. They appear in Roman history in the 2nd century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Salassi controlled the routes over the Alpine passes, charging tolls on travellers and armies. They worked gold deposits in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dora-baltea">Dora Baltea</a> valley by washing, and their disputes with Roman contractors over water rights, recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a>, led to conflict. They lived in villages and fortified places and had no known central capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appius-claudius-pulcher-consul-143-bce">Appius Claudius Pulcher</a> fought them in 143 BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Eporedia</a> in 100 BCE. In 25 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulus-terentius-varro-murena">Aulus Terentius Varro Murena</a> conquered them for Augustus, selling some 36,000 into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aosta">Augusta Praetoria</a>, modern Aosta, on their land.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 25 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:9.45%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 25 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Italy</dd></dl></aside></div>

